  "body": " Let be a compact hyperkähler manifold such that is IHS. Let be a compact connected special Lagrangian submanifold. Suppose its Poincaré dual, with the calibration orientation, is , where , , and . Then . Write and put and . The submanifold is -holomorphic Lagrangian. The class has type for and satisfies .  Since is calibrated, . Formula implies that and . The restriction of to vanishes, so the same formula gives .  The quaternionic relations give If , then the normalized symplectic form for the unchanged complex structure , expressed in the rotated triple, is Thus is still special Lagrangian for , with its phase changed by . Its volume and orientation do not change.  The choice of gives and . Apply to and . Since , it follows that Condition (iii) of , applied to , makes an -holomorphic Lagrangian submanifold.  The holomorphic symplectic form for is . We have proved . The BBF Hodge decomposition identifies the real classes orthogonal to and its conjugate with . Hence has the required type and positive Kähler pairing.  "
